WEBVTT

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:19.870
What a cruel thing to do
to a child such as this.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:25.210
Well, what will you do?

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:32.470
Will you, too, come with me?

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:44.520
THE 
CASE
 STUDY 
OF 
VANITAS

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:52.280
<i>You're pondering the simple things,</i>
<i>pretty much: human emotions, and love?</i>

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.660
<i>I hope one day you'll understand</i>

00:00:56.660 --> 00:01:01.250
<i>Too many wounds have left you</i>
<i>patched together, a miserable sight</i>

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:06.500
<i>That doesn't even know</i>
<i>the definition of "alive"</i>

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:14.010
<i>No need to say,</i>
<i>"Just the two of us" or anything</i>

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:22.600
<i>I've a feeling we can understand</i>
<i>each other, and that's fine for now</i>

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:31.570
<i>I love this world,</i>
<i>and the light only you give me</i>

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:36.450
<i>Makes the world I see</i>
<i>through these fractured eyes </i>

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:41.120
<i>Look gleaming and bright</i>

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.710
<i>There's no such thing as a sure thing</i>

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:50.460
<i>But you can see me, can't you?</i>

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:59.310
<i>When sky and void meet, look back</i>
<i>because the dreams will come later</i>

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.730
Doctor Moreau!

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:10.030
It's an honor to see you again!

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.030
I figured you'd be here
if you were in Paris.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:14.320
Yes, yes!

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.530
I'm impressed you remembered
the way here, Number 69!

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.250
Hmm? Who might these folks be?

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:24.330
They have weapons in hand.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.290
Friends of yours?

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.880
They're your supporters, Doctor!

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:30.960
Huh?!

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:37.890
On the way here, I told them
of your sublime experiments.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.510
Your ideas truly resonated with them,

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:44.730
so they vowed that they would assist you.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.480
As you can see, they are Chasseurs.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:53.070
They shall prove useful as
both assistants and guards!

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.490
How very...

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:59.240
...splendid!

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:06.160
I applaud you! I applaud you!

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:10.670
What a relief. If you turned out to
be evil-doers bent on capturing me,

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.340
I would have had to kill you.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:16.470
Come, come, everyone! Hurry now!

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:19.390
We must prepare to entertain our guests!

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:22.060
Vanitas, he is...

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.970
With enough flattery,

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:28.770
he'll get so excited, he'll blurt out
things we haven't even asked.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:31.270
What became of the abducted vampires?

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:34.480
Is he the only one behind the abductions?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.110
We'll wring every bit of
information we can out of him.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:42.080
After that, we'll let
the Chasseurs have at him,

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.410
or I will slay him myself.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:52.460
Thank you very much.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:56.720
Are these the enhanced
humans Vanitas spoke of?

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:59.760
Now, allow me to
introduce myself once more!

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.100
My name is Moreau!

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.470
Number 69, no doubt,
already told you, but

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.850
I research vampires here!

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:09.940
Question!

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:10.600
--Yes?!

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.480
--Doctor, Doctor!
--Yes?!

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:11.980
--Yes?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:12.940
--Why are you researching vampires?
--Yes?

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:16.570
--Why are you researching vampires?

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.440
What?

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:21.450
He means such vital information
should be obtained from the source!

00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:25.370
I see! Well, that is a
most commendable attitude!

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.580
The truth is I wish to
become a vampire someday!

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.460
When the Church first approached me,

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:41.890
I assisted in their research on vampires
simply out of intellectual curiosity.

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:44.390
But the more I learned about vampires,

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:48.480
the more I couldn't stop
thinking about one thing!

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.150
And that is vampires
are a new human species,

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:56.520
the very apex of evolution!

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:01.070
That's why I want to cross over
to that side now, now, now!

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.780
Hell's bells!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:07.240
Those fools in the Church
treated me like a lunatic!

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:08.160
Hell's bells!

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.790
Because of them, so much of
my time and effort was wasted!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.380
Damn them!

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:23.930
You have no idea how
truly difficult it's been!

00:05:23.930 --> 00:05:27.560
After the Vampire of the Blue Moon
attacked my laboratory that day

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.640
and stole you children from me...

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.310
There was more than one?

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:38.400
...my creations and my place
of research were destroyed.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.030
That ruckus brought my secret
research to the Church's attention,

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.280
and I was nearly killed!

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.540
It was the worst day ever!

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:53.920
My goodness. I'm so sorry about that.

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.960
No, no, forgive me!
I'm not at all angry at you.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:04.300
Number 69, you were
an outstanding specimen.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.510
You gladly cooperated with
each and every experiment!

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:09.850
You were sliced and diced
to the brink of death,

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:15.270
yet you never complained or cried!

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:19.730
That's why I'm so delighted
that you've returned to me!

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:25.110
You came back to assist
with my work, didn't you?

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.990
Of course, I did, Doctor.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:31.620
The moment I heard of the string
of vampire disappearances in Paris,

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:37.540
I had a feeling it must be you,
fighting to complete your work here.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:42.130
But, Doctor, this is the den of Chasseurs,
the very ones who drove you out.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:47.050
Has being alone not
put you at a disadvantage?

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:48.970
That has not been a problem.

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:55.350
After all, I now have that
exalted personage on my side.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.520
Exalted personage?

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:02.570
That's right! A fabulous kindred spirit
who understands my work and supports me!

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:08.570
Thanks to my savior, I was able
to return to my good old laboratory!

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.990
Who exactly is this person you speak of?

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:17.790
Wrong question. It's the one thing
I must not speak of, even to you.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:20.710
Forget that. Look at this!

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:25.420
Freshly harvested vampire eyeballs!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.800
Before they died and turned to dust,

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.550
I carved off the parts
I need for my experiments.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:35.810
What's this?!

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:40.230
Number 69? Have your
eyes not changed color?

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.190
Yes, they have!

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:45.990
Where once they were deep blue,
they're now light in color,

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.990
like copper sulfate.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:53.620
Is this related to the power possessed
by the Vampire of the Blue Moon?

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:56.870
Well, Number 69?!

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.420
How intriguing.

00:07:58.420 --> 00:08:01.710
How intriguing! How very intriguing!

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.590
Number 69! I need but one!

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:07.840
Do you mind if I gouge out
just one to study?!

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:10.510
Number 69!

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:15.720
What do you think you're doing?

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:16.730
Don't do this.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:20.060
Sorry, but I must.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:24.940
Doctor Moreau, there is
much I'd like to say to you,

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.900
but that incessant 69, 69...

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:32.320
Stop referring to people as numbers!

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.370
Your eyes are red.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.660
You're a vampire?!

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.250
I must thank you, Noé.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:48.380
I was about to murder that man
if you hadn't made a move!

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:49.800
Drat!

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.930
Noé, keep a firm grip on him!

00:08:51.930 --> 00:08:53.890
Oh, um, sure!

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.930
Doctor Moreau, who is that
"exalted personage" you spoke of?!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:01.650
Number 69, 69! Who is this vampire?!
Where did he come from?!

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:04.110
May I dissect him?!

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:08.070
Youch! No! I can't believe this! Stop!

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.040
You're...!

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:21.870
Monsieur Spider! Thank you for saving me!

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.830
That does it, Doctor.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:25.960
I'm destroying your laboratory.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.420
No!

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:30.470
What the devil?!

00:09:30.470 --> 00:09:32.930
Charlatan and Naenia,

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:34.180
the masked man,

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:38.140
and Doctor Moreau are all connected?

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:44.150
Oh dear, it seems
my little friend woke up.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:47.520
Is that the curse-bearer Dante
and company were after?!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.480
It manifested already?!

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.860
Not so fast!

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.740
Oh, before I forget, 69,

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:01.160
how is Number 71 doing?

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:05.420
You know, the one that
was so attached to you?

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:11.050
The Vampire of the Blue Moon
took my 71 from me along with you!

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:14.470
Is he not here with you?

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:16.260
Big Brother.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:20.640
Why do you hate Father so?

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.640
Father is a good person. He rescued
us from Moreau's lab, remember?

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:25.810
Give him back. Give him back.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.770
Give my father back to me!

00:10:30.230 --> 00:10:34.400
Vanitas! What is it? Are you all right?!

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.160
Get a grip!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:52.590
What is... that?

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:01.680
Stand back if you won't help.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.350
What?! You stand back, you fool!

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:09.150
At least tell me what
the devil that thing is!

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:19.700
It is the malnomen
Prédateur, "the shadow."

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:26.830
It ravenously devours
all life in its path.

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:37.050
Inverse operations won't
have any effect on it!

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:40.100
We must get the curse-bearer out of there!

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:41.010
Noé!

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:42.930
How?!

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.950
What an idiot.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:00.120
Tell me.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:04.660
Why are you putting yourself in danger
to help vampires of the crimson moon?

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:08.290
They exiled Father.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:13.550
You're too late, anyway.
Hurry up and tell them.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:21.180
You know you don't want
anyone else to die because of you.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:23.600
Vanitas!

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:24.970
Please, you must get up!

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.850
Vanitas!

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:38.700
Noé, get Roland and
his people out of here.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:44.200
The shadow will vanish once it
consumes the curse-bearer within.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:49.500
Until then, it can't harm anyone
else if we can lock it up in here.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:53.210
You can't save it?

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:56.630
I fear it's too late.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:13:00.630
I don't know how to pry
a curse-bearer out of a shadow.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.930
There's nothing more I can do.

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:05.310
No!

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:08.770
I don't wish to give up yet!

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:16.940
Vanitas.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.150
Wh-What?

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:21.200
What do you suppose
it's like within its maw?

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:22.360
What?!

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:26.370
If we can't do anything
from outside, we'll go inside!

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:29.370
Whoa, whoa, whoa! If it eats you, you die!

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.710
Stay there if you're scared.

00:13:31.710 --> 00:13:34.170
I'll do what I can myself.

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:37.500
Hey, wait! Noé!

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:42.430
Vanitas. What are you, anyway?

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:47.010
Why are you here right now?

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:50.140
I am...

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:54.270
What an idiot.
Why are you even doing this?

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.190
Shut your mouth!

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:03.240
I am a doctor.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:06.990
I'm here to save vampires!

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.580
Roland! A little help!

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.750
Maria, Georges! Bring it down!

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:41.230
There's the curse-bearer
that has manifested Prédateur.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:46.700
Do not fear.

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.450
We can win.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:52.910
If we work together?

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.330
I thought we were goners!

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:42.710
Forgive me for my grandiose
statements a moment ago.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:45.130
I clearly underestimated the situation.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:48.840
I tried to warn you.

00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:57.890
I really don't know why we're still alive.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:00.150
It makes no sense.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:14.490
We managed to save him, Vanitas.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:18.370
But Moreau got away.

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:21.420
Well, that's true, but...

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:27.840
Run for it!

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:36.390
Why did it suddenly explode?

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:38.810
My guess is that if the worst happened,

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:43.770
there was a mechanism in place
to destroy the lab and everything in it.

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:49.490
Noé, these children are among the vampires
Moreau abducted, aren't they?

00:16:49.490 --> 00:16:51.280
That's right.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:54.660
I'll look after them.

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:57.500
The vampires had no part
in this latest incident.

00:16:57.500 --> 00:17:01.250
If anything, we Chasseurs
bungled the whole thing.

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:04.880
We'll turn them over to Count Orlok.

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.670
I swear I shall see it through.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:11.890
You two must flee this place at once.

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:14.850
It matters not why you're here.

00:17:14.850 --> 00:17:17.810
If you enter the Chasseurs'
domain without leave,

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:20.940
you will be captured and questioned.

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:22.980
Go before it's too late.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.020
But, captain!

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.280
Leave the rest to us.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.410
Now go. Hurry.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:41.540
Thank you, Roland!

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:47.840
Let us meet again under the sun.

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:53.090
Now then, Georges, Maria.
I'm placing them in your care.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:55.220
Yes, sir!

00:17:55.220 --> 00:17:57.560
Roland!

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.520
Hello, Olivier!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:07.440
Your hair is always so silky smooth!

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:11.030
This is no time for jokes!

00:18:11.030 --> 00:18:14.700
What caused that tremor?!
What have you done this time?!

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:17.530
I'll file a detailed report later.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:20.040
But forget that for now
and listen, Olivier.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:25.830
You'll never believe this,
but I befriended a vampire.

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.840
He gives me splitting headaches!

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:31.630
Are you all right?
Shall I fetch your medicine?

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:33.800
This is your fault, you fool!

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.140
Do you understand the situation?

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:38.180
If the other Chasseurs find out--

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:39.810
If they find out?

00:18:39.810 --> 00:18:42.810
I'd no longer be welcome here?

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:48.980
I just saw something
spectacular a moment ago.

00:18:56.660 --> 00:19:00.290
A human and a vampire
were laughing together.

00:19:00.290 --> 00:19:02.950
They were truly having fun.

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:07.880
I was taught that humans and vampires
will never understand one another.

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:12.260
I never thought what
I accepted as common sense

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:15.130
could be so easily overturned.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.220
What shall I do, Olivier?

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:20.640
My heart won't stop racing!

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:25.350
Captain!

00:19:25.350 --> 00:19:28.100
What is it?

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.940
Damn him.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:34.530
He really is asking for trouble!

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:52.880
We finally made it out.

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:57.550
Was that really all right?

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:00.640
We left everything for Roland to handle.

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:02.100
Heck if I know.

00:20:02.100 --> 00:20:07.520
There are no more curse-bearers involved,
so I've no further interest in the matter.

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:23.200
I'm certain Vanitas didn't wish to get
involved in this if at all possible.

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:31.790
And yet, he did because
there were curse-bearers.

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:37.970
Perhaps it was his
sense of duty as a doctor.

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.440
I'm exhausted.

00:20:59.030 --> 00:21:01.740
I know.

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:04.280
I am, too.

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:19.380
No, it wasn't duty. It seemed
like a crutch he was leaning on.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:22.890
It matters not what you people want!

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:26.390
I <i>will </i>save the vampires!

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:29.980
I wonder.

00:21:29.980 --> 00:21:33.440
The one who seeks salvation most of all,

00:21:33.440 --> 00:21:35.980
the one who prays for it,

00:21:35.980 --> 00:21:38.860
is it not Vanitas himself?

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:23.420
Doctor Moreau is despondent
after losing his laboratory.

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:26.930
He will be no use to us for the present.

00:23:26.930 --> 00:23:32.390
That vampire... This is all his fault!

00:23:32.390 --> 00:23:35.640
Noé Archiviste.

00:23:37.350 --> 00:23:41.400
Now he shall have to deal with me.
